{"G20300":"<b> ἐκδῐκ-ησία</b>, ἡ, <br /> = {ἐκδίκησις}, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Judg.16.28 (uncertain)\">LXX</a>].","G20301":"<b> ἐκζητ-ητής</b>, οῦ, ὁ, <br /> <b>searcher out,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Bar.3.23. \">LXX</a>]","G20303":"<b> ἐκ-θλῐβή</b>, ἡ, <br /> <b>oppression,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Mic.7.2. \">LXX</a>]","G20304":"<b> ἔκ-θλιψις</b>, εως, ἡ, <br /> <b>squeezing out,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “ἀφορισμοί” 7.85, 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Meteorologica” 342a15, 4th-3rd c.BC: Epicurus Philosophus “Epistulae” 2p.50U. \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; τοῦ λοιποῦ (i.e. οῠρον) [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Galenus Medicus “de Usu Partium” 5.16. \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>affliction, distress,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Eze.12.18. \">LXX</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__III</b></Level2> Grammars, <b>ecthlipsis, ejection</b> of a letter, as σκῆπτρον, σκᾶπτον, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Apollonius Dyscolus Grammaticus “de Conjunctionibus;” 230.10, etc.\">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]; also, <b>elision,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 12th c.AD: Eustathius Episcopus Thessalonicensis 984.15 (_plural_). \">Refs</a>]","G20305":"<b> ἐκκοσμ-έω</b>, <br /> <b>deck out, adorn,</b> in <i>passive</i>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.6.2, 2nd c.AD: Aristides Rhetor 1.148 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus \">LXX+1st c.AD+</a>]","G20306":"<b> ἔκλαμπ-ρος</b>, ον, <br /> <b>very bright,</b> φλόγες [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Wis.17.5, cf. Scholia 4th-3rd c.BC: Aratus Epicus 169 \">LXX+4th c.BC+</a>]: <i>neuter</i> as <i>adverb</i>, ἔκλαμπρον γελᾶν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Athenaeus Epigrammaticus 4.158d \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]. Regul. <i>adverb</i> <b>-ρως</b> <b>brilliantly,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" Annuario 3.151 (Pisidia, ἐγλ-lapis). \">Refs</a>]","G20307":"<b> ἔκλαμψις</b>, εως, ἡ, <br /> <b>shining forth, brightness,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.2Mac.5.3; ἡλίου 6th c.AD: Olympiodorus Philosophus “in Aristotelis Meteora commentaria - pars” 49.9. \">LXX+6th c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <i>metaphorically</i>, <b>sudden development,</b> at puberty, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “ἐπιδημίαι” 6.114 (ἐκλάμψιας (_accusative_ _plural_) cited in 2nd c.AD: Galenus Medicus (at [prev. work])). \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]","G20308":"<b> ἐκλεκτ-όω</b>, <br /> in <i>passive</i>, <b>to be separated,</b> i.e.<b>purified,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Isa.52.11. \">LXX</a>]","G20309":"<b> ἐκλεπ-ίζω</b>, <br /> ={ἐκλέπω}, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “περὶ φύσιος παιδίου” 29 (_passive_), 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 1.345 (quoting LXX.Gen.30.37, where LXX λεπίζω). \">LXX+5th c.BC+</a>]","G20310":"<b> ἐκλικμάω</b>, <br /> <b>winnow, sift, empty,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Jdt.2.27, LXX.Wis.5.23. \">LXX</a>]","G20311":"<b> ἐκλογ-ιστής</b>, οῦ, ὁ, <br /> <b>accountant,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Tob.1.22 \">LXX</a>]; as public official, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “Milet.” 7.60 (from Didyma), “PTeb.” 72.449 (2nd c.BC), “AJA” 18.324 (Sardes, 1st c.BC), “CIG” “Corpus Inscriptionum Graecarum” “Corpus Inscriptionum Graecarum” 4956.36 (Oasis Thebarum, 1st c.AD), etc. \">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> ={ἐκλογεύς},{φόρων} [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 1.338. \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]","G20312":"<b> ἐκλογ-ιστία</b>, ἡ, <br /> <b>reckoning: accounts,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Tob.1.21, “Sammelb.” 4423. \">LXX</a>]","G20313":"<b> ἐκμελίζω</b>, <br /> <b>dismember,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.10.5, 8. \">LXX</a>]","G20314":"<b> ἐκπαίζω</b>, <br /> <b>laugh to scorn, mock at,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.1Esd.1.49(51), 1st c.BC: Philodemus Gadarensis Epigrammaticus “Rh.” 2.216S. \">LXX+1st c.BC+</a>]","G20315":"<b> ἐκπετ-άννῡμι</b>, <br /> <i>future</i> -πετάσω, <b>spread out,</b> of a sail, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Iphigenia Taurica” 1135 (Lyric poetry); πώγωνα 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Tim.” 54; χεῖρας LXX.Isa.65.2 \">LXX+5th c.BC+</a>]; of wings, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\"“Anthologia Graeca” 5.178.10 (1st c.BC: Meleager Epigrammaticus); τὰ ὦτα ἐξεπετάννυτο ὥσπερ σκιάδειον 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Equites” 1348 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; of a net, τὸ δὲ δίκτυον ἐκπεπέτασται Oracle texts cited in [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.62 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; στέφος ἐξεπέτασσε <b>scattered</b> it <b>to the winds,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.BC: Bion Bucolicus 1.88. \">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> <i>metaphorically</i>, ἐπὶ κῶμον ἐκπετασθείς <b>wholly given up to</b> the revel, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Cyclops” 497 (Lyric poetry): \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]<i>perfect</i> <i>participle</i> <i>passive</i> ἐκπεπταμένος <b>wide open,</b> κοῖλα καὶ ἐ. [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “περὶ ἀρχαίης ἰητρικῇς” 22 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; of <b>gaping</b> wounds, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. author] “Off.” 11; ἐ. τοῖς βλεφάροις 2nd-3rd c.AD: Aelianus “De Natura Animalium - Ar.Byzantine Epit.” 2.12. \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]","G20316":"<b> ἐκπῐ-άζω</b>, <br /> ={ἐκπιέζω}, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Josh.6.38, 1st c.BC-1st c.AD: Strabo Geographus 16.2.43, “PHolm.” 18.18. \">LXX+1st c.BC+</a>]","G20317":"<b> ἐκπολῑτεύω</b>, <br /> <b>change the constitution of a state, cause it to degenerate,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.4.19. \">LXX</a>]","G20318":"<b> ἐκρῑζ-ωτής</b>, οῦ, ὁ, <br /> <b>rooter out, destroyer,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.3.5. \">LXX</a>]","G20319":"<b> ἐκσᾰόω</b>, <br /> <i>Epic dialect</i> for ἐκσῴζω, ἐξεσάωσεν ὀϊόμενον θανέεσθαι [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 4.12; ἐξεσάωσε θαλάσσης 8th c.BC: Odyssea Homerus Epicus “Odyssey” 4.501 \">Refs 8th c.BC+</a>]; ψυχὴν δ᾽ ἐξ. variant in [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 7th c.BC: Archilochus Lyricus 6; [πέδιλον] ὑπ᾽ ἰλύος 3rd c.BC: Apollonius Rhodius Epicus 1.10. \">Refs 7th c.BC+</a>]","G20320":"<b> ἐκσπονδῠλίζω</b> <br /> or <b>ἐκσφονδ-</b>, <b>break the vertebrae,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.11.18: condemned by “Etymologicum Magnum” 324.44. \">LXX</a>]","G20321":"<b> ἐκσῡρίζω</b>, <br /> <i>Attic dialect</i> <b>ἐκσυρίττω</b>, <i>future</i> ἐκσυριῶ [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Sir.22.1 \">LXX</a>]: <i>aorist 1</i> ἐξεσύρισα [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd-3rd c.AD: Dio Cassius Historicus 51.17 \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]:—<b>hiss off the stage,</b> τινά [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 19.337, 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Nigr.” 9 \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]:—<i>passive</i>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Antiphanes Comicus 191.21. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> <b>hiss loudly,</b> D.C.[same place]","G20322":"<b> ἐκτοπ-ίζω</b>, <br /> <b>remove from</b> a place, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “PTeb.” 38.18 (2nd c.BC, _passive_), etc.\">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]; ἐ. ἑαυτούς <b>take</b> themselves <b>off</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Mirabilia” 842b12, 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 1.74.7, LXX.2Mac.8.13 \">LXX+4th c.BC+</a>]; ἐκτετοπισμένα <b>remote regions</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC-1st c.AD: Strabo Geographus 3.4.19 \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]; Ὅμηρος ἐκτοπίζει τὸν Ἰάσονος πλοῦν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\"Scholia 5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “P.” 4.370, compare 2nd c.AD: Maximus Tyrius Sophista 14.2 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; ἄνθρωποι -τετοπισμένοι τῆς καθ᾽ ἡμᾶς οἰκουμένης <b>outside the bounds of</b> our world, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.AD: Proclus Philosophus “in Platonis Cratylum commentaria” p.74P. \">Refs 5th c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> <i>metaphorically</i>, ἐ. εἰς μῦθον <b>pervert</b> into a fable, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC-1st c.AD: Strabo Geographus 4.1.7. \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <i>intransitive</i>, <b>take oneself from a place, go abroad</b>, like{ἀποδημέω}, οἱ ἐκτοπίζοντες τύραννοι ἀπὸ τῆς οἰκείας [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Politica” 1314b9, etc. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]; of birds of passage and fish, <b>to migrate</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. author] “HA” 600a14. \">Refs</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__II.2</b></Level3> <i>metaphorically</i>, of a speaker, <b>travel far</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. author] “Rh.” 1414b28. \">Refs</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__III</b></Level2> <b>avoid, shun</b>, τὸν πολιτισμόν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 3rd c.AD(?): Diogenes Laertius 4.39. \">Refs 3rd c.AD+</a>]","G20323":"<b> ἐκφλέγω</b>, <br /> <b>to set on fire</b>: <i>metaphorically</i>, τὴν πόλιν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Pax” 608, LXX.4Mac.16.3:—\">LXX+5th c.BC+</a>]<i>passive</i>, <i>metaphorically</i>, ἐκφλέγεσθαι τὴν διάνοιαν <b>to be inflamed</b>.., [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus 2.766a. \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> <b>warm up</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Aretaeus Medicus “περὶ αἰτιῶν καὶ σημείων ὀξέων παθῶν” 2.1. \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]","G20324":"<b> ἐκφόρτιον</b>, <br /> <i>falsa lectio</i> for{ἐκφόριον}[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1, LXX.Deu.28.33. \">LXX</a>]","G20325":"<b> ἐκφῠγή</b>, ἡ, <br /> <b>escape</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.3Mac.4.19. \">LXX</a>]","G20326":"<b> ἐκχάσκω</b>, <br /> in <i>perfect</i> ἐκκέχηνα, <b>gape, gaze</b>, εἴς τινα [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.1Esd.4.19. \">LXX</a>]","G20327":"<b> ἐκχολ-άω</b>, <br /> <b>to be angry</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.3Mac.3.1. \">LXX</a>]","G20328":"<b> ἐλαττον-όω</b>, <br /> <b>diminish</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Pro.14.34, +others\">LXX</a>]:—<i>passive</i>,[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\"LXX.Gen.8.3, 18.28. \">LXX</a>]","G20329":"<b> ἐλεάω</b>, <br /> later form of ἐλεέω, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “Etymologicum Magnum” 327.29, LXX.Pro.21.26 \">LXX</a>].","G20330":"<b> ἐλε-ημοποιός</b>, όν, <br /> <b>giving alms</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Tob.9.6. \">LXX</a>]","G20331":"<b> ἐλευστέον</b>, <br /> (ἔρχομαι) <b>one must come</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.2Mac.6.17. \">LXX</a>]","G20332":"<b> ἐλεφαντ-άρχης</b>, ου, ὁ, <br /> <b>commander of a squadron of sixteen elephants</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC: Asclepiodotus Tacticus “Tact.” 9, 3rd c.BC: Phylarchus Historicus 31 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus, 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Demetrius” 25, LXX.2Mac.14.12. \">LXX+3rd c.BC+</a>]","G20333":"<b> ἐμβῐ-ωσις</b>, εως, ἡ, <br /> <b>maintenance of life</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Sir.38.14. \">LXX</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> <b>way of living</b>,[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\"LXX.3Mac.3.23. \">LXX</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>taking root</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus 2.640d. \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]","G20334":"<b> ἐμμᾰνής</b>, ές, <br /> <b>frantic, raving</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 3.25, 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Ichn.” 15, etc.; ἐμμανεῖ σκιρτήματι 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Prometheus Vinctus” 675 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; ἀοίνοις ἐμμανεῖς θυμώμασιν <b>maddened by</b>.., [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. author] “Eu.” 860 \">Refs</a>]; θεοῦ πνοαῖσιν ἐ. [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Bacchae” 1094; ἐ. Ἥρας ὕπο [prev. author] “Cyc.” 3; ὥσπερ ἐ. ἐπεισπεσών 4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus “Σαμία” 200 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; of elephants in the rutting season, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Historia Animalium” 571b34; κῶμαι LXX.Wis.14.23 \">LXX+4th c.BC+</a>]: <i>comparative</i> <b>-έστερος</b>[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Am.” 14 \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]: <i>superlative</i> -έστατος, ἔρωτες [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 734a, compare 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Aratus” 17 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]. <i>adverb</i> <b>-νῶς</b>[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd-3rd c.AD: Dio Cassius Historicus 65.16; ἐρᾶν 4th-5th c.AD: Eunapius Historicus “Vitae Sophistarum” p.455B. \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]: <i>superlative</i> -έστατα, ἐρῶν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus 336. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]","G20335":"<b> ἐμμελέτ-ημα</b>, ατος, τό, <br /> <b>that on which an art is practised</b>, χρυσὸν καὶ ἄργυρον, τέχνης ἐ. [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Wis.13.10 \">LXX</a>]; <b>instrument for practice</b>, τῆς πάρος ἁρμονίης [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “Anthologia Graeca” 6.83 (1st c.AD(?): Macedonius Epigrammaticus). \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]","G20336":"<b> ἐμπαρρησιάζομαι</b>, <br /> <b>speak freely against</b>, τινί [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 38.12.7. \">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> τῇ προαιρέσει τῆς ἐπιβουλῆς -σάμενοι <b>drawing courage</b> from their purpose <b>to speak openly</b> of the plot, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus “Antiquitates Judaicae” 15.8.4. \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__III</b></Level2> <i>absolutely</i>, ἐ. ἔναντι Κυρίου [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Job.22.26. \">LXX</a>]","G20337":"<b> ἐμπειρ-έω</b>, <br /> <b>to be experienced in, have knowledge of</b>, with <i>genitive</i> <i>of things</i>, τῆς χώρας [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 3.78.6, etc.; τῆς ὁδοῦ LXX.Tob.5.6. \">LXX+2nd c.BC+</a>]","G20338":"<b> ἐμ-πληθύνομαι</b>, <br /> <b>to be filled with</b>, ἀλογιστίας [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.3Mac.5.42. \">LXX</a>]","G20339":"<b> ἐμποδ-ιστικός</b>, ή, όν, <br /> <b>trammelling</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ethica Nicomachea” 1153b2, “Ph.” 215b11, 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 5.16.6, 1st c.BC: Philodemus Gadarensis Epigrammaticus “D.” 3.9, LXX.4Mac.1.4, 2nd c.AD: Marcus Antoninus Imperator 8.41. \">LXX+4th c.BC+</a>]","G20340":"<b> ἐμπολῐορκέω</b>, <br /> <b>besiege in</b> a place, in <i>passive</i>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC-1st c.AD: Strabo Geographus 6.2.6; ὑπό τινος [prev. author] 16.2.9 \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]:—<i>active</i>, ἐνισχύσας πόλιν -ῆσαι [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Sir.50.4. \">LXX</a>]","G20341":"<b> ἔμπονος</b>, ον, <br /> <b>patient of labour</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “Aër.” 12; ἀρετῆς ἔργα φέρει ἔμπονος ἥβη poetical cited in Scholia Heph.p.286C.; ἔμπονοι κόπῳ 2nd c.BC: Ezekiel Poeta Judaeus “Exagoge - Mnemosyne” 208. \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>toilsome, painful</b>, τὰ ἔμπονα [<a href=\"jav