ander Rhetor \">LXX+2nd c.AD+</a>]","G20379":"<b> ἐνυψόω</b>, <br /> <b>exalt, excite,</b> in <i>passive</i>, -ούμενος ὑπὸ τοῦ οἴνου [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Dan.5.1. \">LXX</a>]","G20380":"<b> ἐξάδελφος</b> [ᾰ], ὁ, ἡ, <br /> <b>cousin-german</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “TAM” 2.224 (from Sidyma): _feminine_ also ἐξαδέλφη “CIG” “Corpus Inscriptionum Graecarum” “Corpus Inscriptionum Graecarum” 3891 (from Eumenia). \">Refs</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>nephew,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Tob.1.22(25), 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus “Antiquitates Judaicae” 20.10.3. \">LXX+1st c.AD+</a>]","G20381":"<b> ἐξαλλοι-όω</b>, <br /> <b>change, alter,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.3Mac.3.21 \">LXX</a>]:—<i>passive</i>, <b>change utterly,</b> πρὸς τὸ χεῖρον [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th-3rd c.BC: Theophrastus Philosophus “de Causis Plantarum” 2.15.2, compare 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 1.674. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]","G20382":"<b> ἐξαλλοτρι-όω</b>, <br /> <b>export,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC-1st c.AD: Strabo Geographus 5.1.9. \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>divert, alienate,</b> πόρον εἰς ἑτέρας χρείας [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “BSA” 17.229 (Pamphyl.), compare “PGiss.” 2.24 (2nd c.BC). \">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__II.2</b></Level3> <b>alienate, estrange,</b> τὸν πολιτικὸν ὄχλον [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC: Dionysius Halicarnassensis 11.39; τοὺς πολλοὺς πρὸς τοὺς ἀρίστους 2nd c.AD: Sextus Empiricus Philosophus “adversus Mathematicos” 2.42 \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]:—<i>passive</i>, <b>to be estranged,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.1Mac.12.10. \">LXX</a>]","G20383":"<b> ἐξαπο-στολή</b>, ἡ, <br /> <b>sending away,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" Inscriptiones Graecae 2.985 A 1 (2nd c.BC), 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 1.66.2, LXX.3Mac.4.4; ἐ. θανάτου 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 1.233: _plural_, 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 9.5.5. \">LXX+2nd c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>discharge</b> of an engine or projectile, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 3rd-2nd c.BC: Philo Mechanicus “(Belopoeica) Excerpte aus Philons Mechanik - Ath. Berl. Akad.” 53.46, 2nd-1st c.BC(?): Hero Mechanicus “Belopoeica” 79.4, 110.10. \">Refs 3rd c.BC+</a>]","G20384":"<b> ἔξαρθρ-ος</b>, ον, <br /> (ἄρθρον) <b>dislocated,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.9.13, 2nd c.AD: Galenus Medicus 6.10; τοῦ σκέλους ἔξαρθρος γενέσθαι 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus “Antiquitates Judaicae” 3.11.6. \">LXX+1st c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>with distorted, clumsy joints,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “περὶ ἄρθρων ἐμβολῆς” 10 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; <b>loose-jointed,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Galenus Medicus 1.178. \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]","G20385":"<b> ἐξαρθρ-όω</b>, <br /> <b>dislocate,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.10.5. \">LXX</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> ἐξηρθρωμένος, =[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" {ἔξαρθρος} 11, ἐπωμίδες 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Physiognomonica” 810b35. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]","G20386":"<b> ἐξατῑμ-άζω</b>, <br /> <b>dishonour utterly,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Oedipus Coloneus” 1378, variant in LXX.1Ki.17.42 \">LXX+5th c.BC+</a>]:— also <b>ἐξατῑμ-ατῑμάω</b> (assuming variant) [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC: Philodemus Gadarensis Epigrammaticus “Rh.” 2.174S. \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]","G20387":"<b> ἐξαφ-ίημι</b>, <br /> <b>send forth, discharge,</b> [παλτόν] [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “de Equitandi ratione” 12.12 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; <b>dispatch,</b> γροσφομάχους [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 10.39.1 \">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]; <b>let go</b> an elastic board, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 6th c.AD: Aëtius Medicus 6.87. \">Refs 6th c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>set free from,</b> ἐξαφεῖται τοῦδε (i.e. τοῦ πονεῖν) [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Trachiniae” 72, compare 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus “Antiquitates Judaicae” 18.1.1 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; <b>set free,</b> ἐ. σῶον [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.2Mac.12.24 \">LXX</a>]; <b>let loose,</b> ἀγέλας εἰς καρπούς [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “PLips.” 35.8 (4th c.AD)\">Refs 4th c.AD+</a>]:—<i>passive</i>, <b>to be allowed to escape,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus “Bellum Judaicum” 4.6.3. \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__III</b></Level2> <b>squander,</b> πλοῦτον [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Ichn.” 156. \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]","G20388":"<b> ἐξαφ-ίστημι</b>, <br /> <b>remove,</b> αἱ ἁμαρτίαι.. ἐξαπέστησαν τὰ ἀγαθὰ ἀφ᾽ ὑμῶν variant in [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Jer.5.25. \">LXX</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__2</b></Level3> <b>dispatch,</b> ἐφ᾽ οὓς καθήκει [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “BGU” 1253.16 (2nd c.BC). \">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <i>passive</i>, with <i>aorist</i> 2, <i>perfect</i>, and <i>pluperfect</i> <i>active</i>, <b>depart</b> or <b>withdraw from,</b> τινός [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Oedipus Coloneus” 561, 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Iphigenia Aulidensis” 479 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; <b>grow out of,</b> ἡλικίας [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “PLond.” 5.1708.263 (6th c.AD). \">Refs 6th c.AD+</a>]","G20389":"<b> ἐξέλευσις</b>, εως, ἡ, <br /> later word for ἔξοδος, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.2Ki.15.20 \">LXX</a>].","G20390":"<b> ἐξευμεν-ίζω</b>, <br /> <b>propitiate,</b> θεόν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus “Antiquitates Judaicae” 8.13.8 \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]:—<i>middle</i>,[<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. work] 12.2.14, LXX.4Mac.4.11, 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Fabius Maximus” 4, 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 2.2, +others, 5th c.AD: Hermias Alexandrinus Philosophus “in Platonis Phaedrum scholia” p.89A.:—\">LXX+1st c.AD+</a>]<i>passive</i>, ὑπό τινος, περί τινος, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 2.520, 533, compare 3rd c.AD: Porphyrius Tyrius Philosophus “de Abstinentia - Porphyrii Opuscula” 2.37. \">Refs 1st c.AD+</a>]","G20391":"<b> ἐξευ-φραίνομαι</b>, <br /> <b>to be delighted,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" Corp.Herm. 1.30. \">Refs</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>show rejoicing,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Eze.23.41 (variant). \">LXX</a>]","G20392":"<b> ἐξημερ-όω</b>, <br /> <b>tame</b> or <b>reclaim entirely,</b> χῶρον [ἀκανθώδη] [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.126 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; ἐ. γαῖαν <b>free</b> the land <b>from wild beasts,</b> etc., [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hercules Furens” 20, 852 \">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; <b>reclaim</b> wild plants, κοτίνους εἰς συκᾶς ἐ. [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Fabius Maximus” 20, compare 4th-3rd c.BC: Theophrastus Philosophus “Historia Plantarum” 2.2.12 (_passive_), +others\">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]: <i>metaphorically</i>, <b>soften, humanize,</b> τὸ τῆς ψυχῆς ἀτέραμνον [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 4. 21.4; διανοίας 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 2.402; τὰς τῶν ἠθῶν καὶ παθῶν ὕλας LXX.4Mac.1.29; αὑτὸν διὰ παιδείας 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Numa” 3; τὴν νῆσον ἐξηγριωμένην ὑπὸ κακῶν.. ἐξημέρωσε [prev. author] “Tim.” 35, compare 1st c.BC: Parthenius Mythographus 20.1 \">LXX+2nd c.BC+</a>]; ἡ ἐξημερωμένη ἐν τοῖς νῦν χρόνοις ἀναστροφή our present <b>civilized</b> life, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC: Philodemus Philosophus “περὶ τῶν Στωικῶν” 339.19. \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]","G20393":"<b> ἐξηχ-ευη</b>, <br /> <b>stupes,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “Corpus Glossariorum Latinorum” (to be read -εύῃ). \">Refs</a>]","G20394":"<b> ἐξῐσ-άζω</b>, <br /> <b>make equal,</b> τοῖς ἐνθυμήμασι τὴν λέξιν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 7th c.AD: Stephanus Medicus “in Hp.” 1.57 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator; σεαυτὸν τῷ θεῷ “Corpus Hermeticum” 11.20, cf. Scholia 8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 13.745 \">Refs 8th c.BC+</a>]:—<i>middle</i>, <b>make oneself equal,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Sir.35(32).9(13).\">LXX</a>]—<i>passive</i>, <b>to be equal,</b> τῇ Ἰνδικῇ [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 1st c.BC-1st c.AD: Strabo Geographus 2.1.31. \">Refs 1st c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <i>active</i> <i>intransitive</i>, <b>to be equal,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. author] 17.3.1, 2nd c.AD: Hermogenes Rhetor “περὶ τῶν στάσεων” 1, 6th c.AD: Olympiodorus Philosophus “in Aristotelis Meteora commentaria - pars” 158.15. \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__II.2</b></Level3> <b>to be coextensive,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 6th c.AD: Asclepius Philosophus “in Aristotelis Metaphysicorum libros A-Z commentaria - pars” 381.31, 5th c.AD: Proclus Philosophus “in Platonis Parmenidem commentarii” p.857S., 5th-6th c.AD: Damascius Philosophus “de Principiis” 144; ταῦτα ἀλλήλοις ἐξισάζει 5th c.AD: Proclus Philosophus \">Refs 5th c.AD+</a>]<b>in R.</b>1.29K.","G20395":"<b> ἐξιστάνω</b>, <br /> later form of ἐξίστημι, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.3Mac.1.25, 1st c.AD: Dioscorides (Dioscurides) Medicus 4.73\">LXX+1st c.AD+</a>]:—also <b>ἐξιστάω</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" NT.Act.8.9 \">NT</a>].","G20396":"<b> ἐξοδ-εύω</b>, <br /> <b>march out,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 5.94.7, LXX.1Esd.4.23, 1st c.BC: Diodorus Siculus Historicus 19.63, 2nd c.BC: Nicander Epicus 5th-6th c.AD: Damascius Philosophus 92 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus, etc.\">LXX+2nd c.BC+</a>]; simply, <b>depart,</b> εἰς Τεβτῦνιν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “PTeb.” 55.3 (2nd c.BC)\">Refs 2nd c.BC+</a>]; εἰσοδεύειν καὶ ἐ. ingress and <b>egress</b>, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" “CPR” 187.13 (2nd c.AD). \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> <b>depart this life,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Josh.5.27 (_passive_). \">LXX</a>]","G20397":"<b> ἐξολεθρ-ευμα</b>, ατος, τό, <br /> <b>destruction,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.1Ki.15.21. \">LXX</a>]","G20398":"<b> ἐξομβρ-έω</b>, <br /> <b>pour out like rain,</b> γνῶσιν, βδέλυγμα, [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.Sir.1.19, 10.13. \">LXX</a>]","G20399":"<b> ἐξόμνῡμι</b> <br /> and <b>ἐξομνύω</b>, <i>future</i> ἐξομοῦμαι: <i>aorist</i> ἐξώμοσα:— <b>swear in excuse,</b> ἐξώμοσεν ἀρρωστεῖν τουτονί [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 19.124. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__II</b></Level2> mostly, <b>swear in the negative,</b> ἐξομῇ τὸ μὴ εἰδένα; [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Antigone” 535; μαρτυρεῖν ἢ ἐξομνύειν 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 29.20:\">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>] — mostly in <i>middle</i>, <i>aorist</i> ἐξωμοσάμην, <b>deny</b> or <b>disown upon oath, swear formally that one does not know</b> a thing, <b>abjure,</b> τὰς διαβολάς [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" [prev. author] 57.36; ἃ μὲν οἶδεν ἐξόμνυσθαι 4th c.BC: Isaeus Orator 9.19: _absolutely_, [prev. work] 18, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 949a, etc.; οὐκ ἂν ἐξομόσαιτο μὴ οὐκ εἰδέναι 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 57.59, compare “PHal.” 1.230 (3rd c.BC)\">Refs 5th c.BC+</a>]; <b>forswear, renounce,</b> συγγένειαν ἐξόμνυσθαι [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" LXX.4Mac.4.26, 10.3. \">LXX</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__II.2</b></Level3> <b>decline</b> or <b>refuse</b> an office <b>by an oath</b> that one has not means or health to perform it, ἐξομόσασθαι τὴν πρεσβείαν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Aeschines Orator 2.94, compare 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 19.124 \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]; [τὴν ἀρχήν] [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Politica” 1297a20, 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Marcellus” 6, 12, compare 4th-3rd c.BC: Theophrastus Philosophus “Characteres” 24.5. \">Refs 4th c.BC+</a>]<br /><Level3><b>__II.3</b></Level3> <b>forswear, renounce,</b> τὴν ἐλευθερίαν [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Apol.” 6; τὴν ἐπικουρίαν 4th c.AD: Julianus Imperator “Orationes” 2.60d. \">Refs 2nd c.AD+</a>]<br /><Level2><b>__III</b></Level2> later, simply, <b>swear, make affidavit,</b> [<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" title=\" PFlor. 32 A 12 (3rd c.AD). \">Refs 3rd c.AD+</a>]"}